  "content": {
    "id": "p13-challenge-q2",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "In a raffle, 50 tickets are sold. The tickets are numbered from 1 to 50. They are placed in a hat and one is drawn out at random to win a prize.\n\nSuppose that the raffle tickets are coloured: those numbered 1 to 25 are green, the tickets numbered 26 to 40 are yellow and the rest are blue. Find the probability that the ticket that wins the prize:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p13-challenge-q2-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "is blue",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{1}{5}$",
          "worked": "The blue tickets are numbered 41 to 50: ten tickets.\n$$P(\\text{blue})=\\frac{10}{50}=\\frac{1}{5}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-challenge-q2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "is not green",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{1}{2}$",
          "worked": "There are 25 green tickets.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{not green})&=1-\\frac{25}{50}\\\\P(\\text{not green})&=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-challenge-q2-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "is green or blue",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{7}{10}$",
          "worked": "There are 25 green and 10 blue tickets, with no overlap.\n$$P(\\text{green or blue})=\\frac{25+10}{50}=\\frac{7}{10}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-challenge-q2-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "is both green and blue",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0$",
          "worked": "Each ticket has only one colour, so no ticket is both green and blue.\n$$P(\\text{green and blue})=\\frac{0}{50}=0$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 16
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-challenge-q2-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "is even-numbered and blue",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{1}{10}$",
          "worked": "The favourable tickets are $42,44,46,48,50$.\n$$P(\\text{even and blue})=\\frac{5}{50}=\\frac{1}{10}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-challenge-q2-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "is prime and yellow",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{3}{50}$",
          "worked": "Among the yellow numbers 26 to 40, the primes are $29,31,37$.\n$$P(\\text{prime and yellow})=\\frac{3}{50}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      }
    ]
  },
